{% extends "layout.html" %}

{% block title %}About — IVS Advisors{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f2efeb] text-black pt-32 px-6 sm:px-16 md:px-24 lg:px-32 pb-20">
  
<h1 class="text-4xl font-light tracking-wide uppercase mb-12 text-center">
    Vetia Searcy
  </h1>
  <!-- Image and bio block -->
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center md:items-start gap-10">
    
    <!-- Image -->
    <div class="flex-shrink-0">
      <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='vetia.png') }}" alt="Vetia Searcy" class="w-72 h-auto rounded-md shadow-md" />
    </div>
    
    <!-- Text -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <p><strong>Vetia Searcy</strong> is the Founder and Principal of <em>ILS Corporate Services, LLC</em> (est. 2005) and <em>IVS Advisors</em>, harnessing over 15 years of experience in corporate, finance, and real estate transactions. She holds a unique industry perspective having worked on all three sides of New Markets Tax Credits (NMTC) transactions.</p>

      <p>As a <strong>CDE Consultant</strong>, Ms. Searcy supervised preparation of 4 successful NMTC award applications, closed on over $267MM in NMTC transactions, managed compliance procedures, and sourced allocation for national and local CDEs. As <strong>Vice President of Community Development Tax Credits</strong> at JPMorgan Chase, she originated, underwrote, structured, and closed over $200MM in NMTC and hybrid NMTC/Historic & NMTC/LIHTC transactions, increasing closings in her coverage area by over 100%.</p>

      <p>As a <strong>Project Consultant</strong>, she uses her expertise to guide CEOs, CFOs, and Project Managers through the NMTC closing process, specializing in sourcing allocation for rural, metro, and underserved communities.</p>

      <p>During New York State on PAUSE, she volunteered her expertise to advise under-banked, minority independent contractors and small businesses, connecting them to community-based banks that could assist with PPP loans.</p>

      <p>Ms. Searcy is a graduate of Columbia College, Columbia University. She is an active participant in NMTC panel presentations across the U.S. Notable awards include the <em>Novogradac Non-Metro QLICI of the Year Award</em> (2017) and <em>Honorable Mention</em> for the same category that year.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

